/-!
# Linear defining-field exclusions and original marked consumers

The full B.4.2 linear-two and linear-three rows have degree one, and the
B.4.5 orthogonal row is excluded over its larger defining field. The actual
Sylow-central involution is placed inside K̂ before root-pair geometry is
used. Comparisons retain K̂ ≃ L/Z(L), including the possible center of SL₃.

Binary action coordinates and compatible markings are exported. Their
applications exclude the linear-three row using condition (ii), and the
binary natural four/five rows on the literal original chief sections.
Configuration and compatible faithful-image producers remain explicit.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, B.4.2/B.4.5, printed pp.86–87; 13.5.21,
printed pp.923–924 (PDF pp.940–941).
-/
